{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:fb325631e3915d62","name":"Ion Damage","source":{"id":"source:reference-fb325631e3915d62","title":"Ion Damage","revision":26732,"timestamp":"2025-07-05T16:41:36Z","sha256":"09c9ce834ff4f13cc83637c9d5850ea94bfc40ec67500b62939fca7095a77aae","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=26732","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Ion%20Damage&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-fb325631e3915d62","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Core Rulebook"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Core_Rulebook"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Ion Pistols"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ion_Pistols"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ion Rifles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ion_Rifles"}," emit powerful bursts of electrostatic energy that can disable ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicles"},", and electrical devices in much the same way that ",{"tag":"a","children":["Stun"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Stun"}," weapons can incapacitate living creatures. When you make a successful attack with a weapon that deals Ion Damage, first subtract half of the Ion Damage from the target's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"},". Creatures that do not have a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Cybernetic Prosthesis"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Cybernetic_Prosthesis","referenceId":"reference:06abec99ed18263b"}," are singed by the Ion energy, but suffer no other ill effects.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicles"},", electronic devices, and cybernetically enhanced creatures may suffer additional effects, as noted below:\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":["If the Ion Damage reduces the target's current ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"}," to 0, the target moves -5 steps on the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Condition Track"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Condition_Track"}," and is either ",{"tag":"a","children":["Disabled"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Disabled"}," or knocked ",{"tag":"a","children":["Unconscious"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Unconscious"},"."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":["If the Ion Damage (before being halved) equals or exceeds the target's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Threshold"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Threshold"},", the target moves -2 steps on the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Condition Track"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Condition_Track"},"."]}]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
